How to Read a Balance Sheet — a Sketchnote film

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence texts in fonts/)
- Kalam Bold — Indian Type Foundry — https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/kalam (files from the @fontsource/kalam npm package)
- Patrick Hand — Patrick Wagesreiter — https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/patrickhand (files from the @fontsource/patrick-hand npm package)

Voice
- Kokoro-82M (Apache 2.0), voice bf_emma, through the Lemo-Opuscar library's core/tts/tts.py

Music samples (CC0 1.0), through the Lemo-Opuscar library's core/audio/sampler.py
- marimba, glockenspiel, vibraphone, vibraphone (bowed), harp: Versilian Community Sample Library (Versilian Studios)
- cellos_pizz: VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition (Versilian Studios)
- kalimba: FreePats project (freepats.zenvoid.org)

Drawing engine: the Sketchnote style's Canvas engine from the Lemo-Opuscar library (github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar), MIT licence.

Everything else (drawings, paper, pen and marker sounds, whooshes, score) is generated by the code in this folder.
"Corner Bakery" and its figures are fictional, made up to illustrate the idea.
